    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1301">

                <pb facs="1061" n="1051" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1051"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–1849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-18">January 18,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received January 18—3:47 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>81. Newspaper Tientsin <hi rendition="#italic">Jih Pao</hi> carried following
                    item today:<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1301-f1"/>
                </p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Commander Nieh Jung-chen of the Peiping-Tientsin Garrison Headquarters in a
                        joint statement on January 15 with political member Po Yi-po announced that
                        the Liberation Army will accord protection to law-abiding foreign residents
                        in Tientsin, on the condition that they observe the provisions laid down in
                        the proclamations of the People’s Government, the Military Commission, and
                        the Garrison Headquarters.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1301-f1" n="3" xml:id="d1301-f1-content">
                <p>For information on Communist occupation of Tientsin, see telegram No. 61, January
                    14, 10:45 p. m., <ref target="#pg48">p. 48</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
